    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d785">

                <pb facs="1461" n="1427" sameAs="frus:frus1948v02/pg1427"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Austria)/7–1748:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Legation in Austria
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-07-17T15:00:00-04:00">July 17, 1948—3 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>641. Sov note on Berlin<anchor n="1" xml:id="d785-f1"/> refers twice to Vienna
                    and international agreements concerning Austria, linking Austria with Germany in
                    justifying Sov blockade. We would appreciate your evaluation of these references
                    and your analysis of possible basis for a blockade of Vienna. Although possible
                    Sov action would undoubtedly be based on legal position and charge of violation
                    of international agreements by western states, could such instances as Sov
                    complaints reported in SO–15417 <pb facs="1462" n="1428" xml:id="pg1428"/> July
                        15<anchor n="2" xml:id="d785-f2"/> on air transport difficulties (P–2117 July 14<anchor n="2" xml:id="d785-f3"/>) be
                    utilized by Sovs as cause for aggressive action?</p>
                <p>If you consider Sov blockade likely, Dept requests your and Keyes’ recommendations for counter-action and
                    for steps which might be taken to forestall or delay such a move.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
